<%- include('_legal-open', { legalTitle: 'Cookie Policy', legalLede: 'Every cookie and technology this site actually uses — listed from the live register, not copied from a template.' }) %>
        <nav class="legal-toc" aria-labelledby="toc-title">
          <h2 id="toc-title">On this page</h2>
          <ol>
            <li><a href="#what">What cookies are</a></li>
            <li><a href="#used">What we actually use</a></li>
            <li><a href="#not-used">What we do not use</a></li>
            <li><a href="#register">Full register</a></li>
            <li><a href="#settings">Change your choices</a></li>
            <li><a href="#gpc">Global Privacy Control</a></li>
          </ol>
        </nav>

        <div class="prose">
          <% if (typeof saved !== 'undefined' && saved === '1') { %>
            <div class="alert alert--success" role="status">Your cookie preferences were saved.</div>
          <% } %>
          <% if (typeof withdrawn !== 'undefined' && withdrawn === '1') { %>
            <div class="alert alert--success" role="status">
              Optional consent withdrawn. Analytics and marketing are now off. Your bag and checkout are unaffected.
            </div>
          <% } %>

          <h2 id="what">1. What cookies are</h2>
          <p>
            A cookie is a small file a website stores in your browser. We use them for two kinds of things: keeping the
            shop working (your bag, your sign-in), and remembering the choice you made about everything else.
          </p>

          <h2 id="used">2. What we actually use — three cookies, all first party</h2>
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Cookie</th><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Lifetime</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>an_sid</code></td><td>Strictly necessary</td>
                <td>Your session: the bag, your sign-in, checkout state and the CSRF token that protects forms.
                  HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax so scripts and other sites cannot read it.</td>
                <td>30 days or until you sign out</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>an_consent</code></td><td>Strictly necessary</td>
                <td>Remembers your cookie choices so the banner does not reappear and your settings are honoured.
                  HttpOnly and SameSite=Lax.</td>
                <td>180 days</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><em>none</em></td><td>Analytics</td>
                <td>Counting happens on our own server, so no cookie is needed and no identifier is created.</td>
                <td>—</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p>
            That is the complete list. There is no third-party analytics cookie, no advertising cookie, no session
            replay, no heatmap tool and no social embed.
          </p>

          <h2 id="not-used">3. What we deliberately do not use</h2>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>No Google Analytics or Google Tag Manager.</strong> No snippet, no SDK, no network request.</li>
            <li><strong>No Meta Pixel, TikTok pixel, LinkedIn Insight or any advertising tag.</strong></li>
            <li><strong>No third-party fonts.</strong> Space Grotesk and Inter are self-hosted from this domain, so your
              browser never talks to Google’s font servers.</li>
            <li><strong>No chat widget, no review plugin, no embedded video.</strong></li>
            <li><strong>No fingerprinting, no cross-site identifiers, no data brokers.</strong></li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            We removed these on purpose. Every external script is a company that learns something about your visit, so
            the default here is none. If we ever add one, it must first appear in the register below and stay blocked
            until you consent.
          </p>

          <h2 id="register">4. Full technology register (live from our database)</h2>
          <p class="small">
            This table is generated from the same register the engineering and privacy reviewers use, so it cannot
            drift out of date quietly.
          </p>
          <table>
            <caption class="sr-only">Cookie and third-party technology register</caption>
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Name</th><th scope="col">Provider</th><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Retention</th><th scope="col">Status</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <% trackers.forEach(function (t) { %>
                <tr>
                  <td><strong><%= t.name %></strong></td>
                  <td><%= t.provider %></td>
                  <td><%= t.category %></td>
                  <td><%= t.purpose %></td>
                  <td><%= t.data_collected %><br><span class="small">Cookies: <%= t.cookies %></span></td>
                  <td><%= t.retention %></td>
                  <td>
                    <%= t.status %>
                    <% if (t.status === 'disabled' || t.status === 'removed') { %><br><span class="small muted">Not loaded</span><% } %>
                    <% if (t.status === 'not_configured') { %><br><span class="small muted">Not connected</span><% } %>
                  </td>
                </tr>
              <% }); %>
            </tbody>
          </table>

          <h2 id="settings">5. Change your choices</h2>
          <p>
            Accepting and rejecting are designed to be equally easy: one click each, the same size, on the same screen.
            There is no “confirm rejection” extra step and no pre-ticked optional category.
          </p>
          <div style="display:flex;gap:.6rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:1.25rem 0;">
            <form method="post" action="/consent/accept-all">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
              <button class="btn btn--small" type="submit">Accept all</button>
            </form>
            <form method="post" action="/consent/reject">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
              <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" type="submit">Reject non-essential</button>
            </form>
            <form method="post" action="/consent/withdraw">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
              <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" type="submit">Withdraw all optional consent</button>
            </form>
            <button class="btn btn--ghost btn--small" type="button" data-consent-open="cookies-page">Open preferences</button>
          </div>

          <h2 id="settings-form">Detailed preferences</h2>
          <form id="cookie-settings-form" method="post" action="/consent">
            <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrf %>">
            <input type="hidden" name="source" value="settings-page">
            <% ['necessary','functional','analytics','marketing'].forEach(function (key) {
                 var meta = consentCategories[key]; %>
              <div class="pref-row">
                <div>
                  <h3 id="cs-<%= key %>-label"><%= meta.label %><%= meta.always ? ' (always on)' : '' %></h3>
                  <p><%= meta.description %></p>
                </div>
                <div>
                  <div class="switch">
                    <input type="checkbox" id="cs-<%= key %>" name="<%= key %>" value="1"
                           <%= key === 'necessary' || consent[key] ? 'checked' : '' %>
                           <%= meta.always ? 'disabled' : '' %>
                           aria-labelledby="cs-<%= key %>-label"
                           aria-describedby="cs-<%= key %>-desc">
                    <span class="track" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="thumb" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  </div>
                  <span class="pref-state" id="cs-<%= key %>-desc">
                    <%= key === 'necessary' || consent[key] ? 'On' : 'Off' %>
                  </span>
                </div>
              </div>
            <% }); %>
            <button class="btn mt-2" type="submit">Save preferences</button>
          </form>

          <h2 id="gpc">6. Global Privacy Control</h2>
          <p>
            If your browser sends a Global Privacy Control (GPC) or Do Not Track signal, we treat it as an opt-out of
            analytics and marketing, and we record that in the consent receipt. If a GPC signal is active and you press
            “Accept all”, analytics and marketing are still kept off, and the site tells you that this happened rather
            than quietly overriding your browser.
          </p>

          <h2 id="retention">7. Consent records</h2>
          <p>
            Each time you save a preference we store a receipt: your choices, the time, the policy version, and a
            one-way hash of your IP address and browser string so we can demonstrate consent without keeping your IP
            address itself. Receipts are retained for 180 days on a rolling basis.
          </p>

          <p class="small">
            Related: <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> ·
            <a href="/transparency">Transparency and tracker audit</a> ·
            <a href="/privacy-requests">Privacy &amp; Data Requests</a>
          </p>
        </div>
<%- include('_legal-close') %>
